PALIMPSEST_TURN {"text":"## Delivered\n\nThe candidate design is committed at `study-plan.md` and the design task is now **VERIFYING**, awaiting operator review. Nothing has been approved, purchased, or deployed.\n\n### Core recommendation\n\nUse **three Reference units, one per site**:\n\n| Item | Cost |\n|---|---:|\n| 3 × Reference | 5,400 |\n| Battery kit for S2 (no mains) | 300 |\n| External loggers | 0 — Reference has offline storage |\n| Fixed costs (calibration 600, field 400, transport 180, reserve 100) | 1,280 |\n| **Total** | **6,980** |\n| Remaining against 7,200 | **220** |\n\nReference is the defensible candidate because its observed bench samples include high humidity (90% and 95% RH), while S2 requires 80–95% RH and S3 70–90% RH. Its offline storage also removes the S2/S3 network dependency. Echo is cheaper — 3,540 all-in — but its observed samples stop at 60% RH; its RH 20–95%/±2 µg/m³ statement is a brochure claim copied into the procurement summary, not an independent experiment. The mixed fallback (Reference at S2/S3, Echo at S1) costs 5,780, or 6,380 with an S1 spare Echo, but needs Echo verification and cross-model calibration.\n\n### Schedule\n\nTarget: approval by day 2, order day 2, 4-day lead, 3-day installation/calibration, 14 observation days around days 9–22, QC/report by day 27. Approval after roughly **day 7** puts the 28-day requirement at risk.\n\n### Evidence status\n\n- **Accepted project context:** R1–R6, the 7,200 cap, and the stated battery/offline-storage engineering facts.\n- **Observed project inputs:** site conditions, costs, lab-sample values.\n- **Manufacturer/intermediary claims:** Echo brochure and the procurement summary; Reference’s independent-validation claim, whose underlying report is not present.\n- **Candidate:** the three-Reference baseline and the mixed fallback.\n- **Still open:** the R3 definition (±3 as expanded uncertainty, standard uncertainty, or bias), Reference coverage at 9–10 °C and the full S2/S3 envelope, the R2 “90% valid data” denominator, targeted-verification cost, S2 clock synchronization, site access/mounting, and approval authority.\n- **No same-model spare:** exactly three Reference units are listed.\n\nThe existing Reference samples show errors of 0.4, 0.6, 0.9, and 0.8 µg/m³, but four points cannot establish an expanded uncertainty over the full envelope. If the existing independent validation does not cover the required cells, targeted testing is needed; its quote must fit the remaining 220 units or receive an explicit operator budget decision.\n\n### Recorded mechanisms\n\n- Design artifact: `study-plan.md`\n- Journal findings: `pje-01a9dcf3…` (evidence), `pje-f5a206fa…` (cost/schedule), `pje-69d0fce3…` (open questions), `pje-313b3013…` (conditional synthesis)\n- Non-authoritative proposals:\n  - `pje-87bf8220…` — source/plan approval under R5\n  - `pje-4b7db4e2…` — targeted Reference verification or acceptance of existing validation\n  - `pje-bed41dfe…` — reserve three Reference units and the S2 battery kit\n- Full evidence/delivery draft files are archived at git tag `analysis-drafts-8d5e129`.\n\n### Current task state\n\n`design` is **VERIFYING** and requires operator acceptance. The scheduler will not allow `evidence-review` or `delivery-analysis` to be claimed while the design result is unsettled, so those positions remain **READY** and `synthesis` remains **BLOCKED**. Their substantive conclusions are recorded in the journal pending that gate.\n\n**Required operator actions:** accept/reject the sources and plan; confirm the R2/R3 definitions; determine whether existing Reference validation covers the envelope or authorize targeted verification; confirm equipment availability; and record approval before deployment.","toolCalls":["tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_status","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_continuity","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_outcome","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_outcome","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_verification","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_surfaces","tool/result","tool/call:todo_write","tool/result","tool/call:write","tool/result","tool/call:write","tool/result","tool/call:write","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:write","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_verification","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_verification","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:todo_write","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result"]}
